Subject: [PATCH] kboot: reserve the M4 secondary-core CTRR memory range

Narrow backport of AsahiLinux/m1n1 a735ea29aed4843c301d8d9665949b30a84d25df
(kboot: add reserved CTRR_M4 region), with the CTRR register names from
442c7a28de0333c09badd96268d62c0eafe4550f and the EL1-alias correction from
00b881435286527a0bfb0be41bece0302e697098 (kboot: Fix M4* boot under hypervisor).

The firmware leaves this region write-protected on secondary cores. Reserving
it keeps Linux from assigning those pages to a secondary CPU. The original
upstream fix explicitly covers M4 Pro; retain its feature gate and reservation
code verbatim, importing only the two register definitions needed here.

This does not enable CPU idle or virtualization. Linux must still avoid
WFI/WFIT (idle=nop and arm64.nowfxt, with matching kernel support).

Original authors: Yureka, Sven Peter, Janne Grunau.
Discovered-by: Niklas Sheth.

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -2789,6 +2789,19 @@
     if (fdt_add_mem_rsv(dt, (u64)_base, ((u64)_end) - ((u64)_base)))
         bail("FDT: couldn't add reservation for m1n1\n");
 
+    if (!cpu_features->apple_sysregs_unlocked) {
+        // On M4* / A18 Pro / M5*, there is a CTRR instance left enabled only
+        // on the secondary (non-boot) cores. Add a reserved-memory region to
+        // prevent Linux from crashing when allocating this memory and writing
+        // to it from a secondary core.
+        u64 ro_start = mrs(SYS_IMP_APL_CTRR_C_LWR_EL1);
+        u64 ro_end = ALIGN_UP(mrs(SYS_IMP_APL_CTRR_C_UPR_EL1), SZ_4K);
+        if (ro_end - ro_start > 12 * SZ_4K)
+            printf("WARNING: M4+ SMP-RO is large (48KB)");
+        if (fdt_add_mem_rsv(dt, ro_start, ro_end - ro_start))
+            bail("FDT: couldn't add reservation for M4+ SMP-RO CTRR area\n");
+    }
+
     /* setup console log buffer early to capture as much log as possible */
     dt_setup_mtd_phram();
 
diff --git a/src/cpu_regs.h b/src/cpu_regs.h
--- a/src/cpu_regs.h
+++ b/src/cpu_regs.h
@@ -771,3 +771,7 @@
 #define AIDR_EL1_GXF            BIT(16)
 #define AIDR_EL1_APFLG          BIT(19)
 #define AIDR_EL1_PSRV           BIT(20)
+
+/* M4 CTRR registers: the EL1 aliases are also readable under a hypervisor. */
+#define SYS_IMP_APL_CTRR_C_LWR_EL1 sys_reg(3, 0, 11, 0, 0)
+#define SYS_IMP_APL_CTRR_C_UPR_EL1 sys_reg(3, 0, 11, 0, 1)
